  "tagline": "Java time-series database layered on Cassandra or ScyllaDB, from the OpenTSDB lineage.",
  "description": "KairosDB began in 2013 as a rewrite of OpenTSDB that swapped HBase for Cassandra, keeping the metric-plus-tags model and the telnet and HTTP put APIs while adding a richer JSON query API with aggregators, groupers and rollups. Running on Cassandra or ScyllaDB gives it straightforward horizontal scale and multi-datacenter replication through the underlying store. Development is sporadic: the last stable release, 1.3.0, came out in 2021, and a 1.4.0 beta was tagged in early 2026. It is mainly relevant where a Cassandra cluster already exists and teams want a thin metrics layer on top.",
